# Read by the `scheduler` image (Dockerfile) via busybox crond, which
# forwards the container's own environment to each job — verified against
# plain alpine/crond directly, since that's the one thing that would make
# this silently break (a job that can't see DATABASE_URL fails loudly at
# lib/env's own validation, not silently). Times are UTC.
#
# Every command here is a plain `npm run ...`: single-shot, idempotent per
# its own window (see lib/ops/task-run.ts and lib/ops/scheduled-task.ts), so
# a missed or repeated tick never duplicates work or double-deletes. A
# restart of this container catches up on the next tick, nothing more.
#
# min hour day month weekday  command
0    */6  *   *     *         cd /app && npm run ops:backup
10   3    *   *     *         cd /app && npm run privacy:purge-ip-data
20   *    *   *     *         cd /app && npm run rate-limits:purge
30   3    *   *     *         cd /app && npm run storage:sweep
0    4    2   *     *         cd /app && npm run ops:anonymize-alert
